{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981925-so-about-that-flange","id":981925,"title":"So about that flange","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-04T20:16:52-07:00","id":981925,"title":"So about that flange","content":"I'm getting ready to run a chronicle set in Chicago, while I do have a plot of my own there is that pesky meta plot about a certain piece of Celestial Plumbing floating around. <br /> <br /> Now I don't normally go for the MacGuffin but I'm not about to drop because it makes interesting background noise due to it being the big mystery in Chicago. <br /> <br /> So here's the rub, for the life of me I can't figure out what the flange actually &quot;is&quot; or &quot;should be&quot; if the players decide to segway onto that plot line. Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T23:04:49-07:00","id":981978,"title":"","content":"I can't remember where but I recall reading somewhere that the Flange was connected to the Exarch, the Gate.<br /> \u200bOf course with the Chronicles of Darkness there probably isn't an official, exact answer, just possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T23:10:26-07:00","id":981980,"title":"","content":"A bit of the God-Machine, or a bit of the Celestial Ladder - or both! (Dun dun dun, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T00:43:58-07:00","id":982001,"title":"","content":"You could just leave it blank. It's an artifact that perhaps looks a bit like a flange (ie. a disc with holes in it). Magi are going nuts over it, but it's actually not clear what it is/was and even perhaps what it does.<br /> <br /> Actually, going on from that. Perhaps it's a mage lure. An artifact designed (it probably doesn't matter who by, but it kinda seems a Seer thing to do) to look like some impossibly fascinating mystery, which is actually not solvable. The point is that it would warp the behaviour of the Awakened without the need for any direct magical influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T01:54:46-07:00","id":982017,"title":"","content":"Heck it might not even be an artifact since no one has even found it yet, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:36:35-07:00","id":982118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981925-so-about-that-flange?p=982001#post982001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could just leave it blank. It's an artifact that perhaps looks a bit like a flange (ie. a disc with holes in it). Magi are going nuts over it, but it's actually not clear what it is/was and even perhaps what it does.<br /> <br /> Actually, going on from that. Perhaps it's a mage lure. An artifact designed (it probably doesn't matter who by, but it kinda seems a Seer thing to do) to look like some impossibly fascinating mystery, which is actually not solvable. The point is that it would warp the behaviour of the Awakened without the need for any direct magical influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I like, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:33:00-07:00","id":982193,"title":"","content":"Mages who examined the flange, in records, were clearly impressed at its raw power. Mind-boggling power contained within it, but no reliable records mention how to access its powers or even hint at what they are. <br /> <br /> Different examiners approached things very differently; Theories abound. <br /> <br /> One of which is that the Flange isn't clearly described because it <i>has</i> no specific function on its own. It isn't intrinsically an Iris anywhere. It doesn't even store as much mana as a proper artifact should! No, the Flange is a component of something far greater.<br /> <br /> A paranoiac of this branch theorizes that it's a missing control check for the God Machine, and if properly installed it would allow it direct supernal interaction at the expense of being completely controlled by the Exarch who formed it. In essence, this guy thinks that it's a sort of uber Thumin.<br /> <br /> &quot;Tosh&quot;, claimed another. &quot;Sure, it's obviously a part of something greater, but that means it has some interesting properties. If we can find the other pieces of the system, we can find out what the Flange, itself, does.&quot; This fellow doesn't talk about his pet theory to most, but he thinks that it's probably an artifact that makes creating a stable Iris between locations far easier... locations that needn't be limited to this physical world.<br /> <br /> All of those researchers are obviously wrong: It's a brace from the Celestial Ladder. If properly installed in Chicago and the Tower Perilous, it could halt the destruction, there. Unfortunately, it needs to be placed in three other places, as well, and those have yet to be identified. That's why Fafnir still keeps it secret and safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:03:59-07:00","id":983104,"title":"","content":"Such a great story seed!<br /> <br /> In my old Chicago campaign I treated it like one of the Crystal skulls, and as a Supernal Anchor. One Truth: The Flange ended up being the remnant of elevating this part of the Ladder to the Supernal. The Crystal is what was left to link the artifact back to the fallen world. Opportunity: Use it to construct a Demense. Any Demense it was part of gained a Supernal resonance and temporarily granted the Dream Merit to anyone who meditated for 5 days or more.<br /> <br /> \u200bI also decided that the Flange had 5 holes in it. Each hole resonated with one of the five paths/watch towers. In Game thought: It was suggested that perhaps the Flange was suspended between the watch towers to balance the Ladder without tearing free. Without the Flange the ladder ruptured the Universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:31:22-07:00","id":983117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981925-so-about-that-flange?p=982118#post982118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This I like, thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you go this route, I encourage you to read the story &quot;Crimson Lips&quot; from the Fallen World Chronicle Anthology. Without spoiling it, it's highly relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}